
## Overview

Here's a comprehensive guide provides step-by-step commands and troubleshooting procedures for deploying and maintaining a full Security Orchestration, Automation and Response (SOAR) stack using Wazuh SIEM, TheHive case management platform, and Cortex analyzers. Whether you're setting up your first SOAR environment or troubleshooting integration issues in production, this document covers everything from Docker container management and network connectivity to alert generation and API testing.

**What you'll find in this guide:**

- Docker commands for managing Wazuh, TheHive, and Cortex containers
- Network troubleshooting for VM and container connectivity issues
- Wazuh agent deployment and management (Linux and Windows)
- Custom integration script configuration and testing
- TheHive API operations and alert verification
- Real-world alert generation examples for testing
- Common issues and their solutions
- Quick reference commands for daily operations

This guide is based on real-world deployment experience and addresses common pitfalls encountered when integrating these powerful open-source security tools in a containerized environment.

**Infrastructure Used:**

- Ubuntu 20.04 LTS host (VMware) 
- Docker & Docker Compose 
- Wazuh Manager 4.13.1 
- TheHive 4.1.24-1 
- Cortex (Latest) 
- Elasticsearch & Cassandra versions 
- **Windows Server 2022** as the monitored agent ( more to come )
- VMware networking details
