## 5. Integration Troubleshooting

### Check Integration Configuration

```bash
# View integration block in ossec.conf
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> cat /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf | grep -A 7 "<integration>"
```

### Verify Integration Script

```bash
# Check if script exists
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> ls -la /var/ossec/integrations/custom-w2thive.py

# View script content
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> cat /var/ossec/integrations/custom-w2thive.py

# Check permissions
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> ls -la /var/ossec/integrations/
```

### Install thehive4py

```bash
# Install in Wazuh container
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/framework/python/bin/pip3 install thehive4py==1.8.1

# Verify installation
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/framework/python/bin/pip3 list | grep thehive
```

### Test Integration Manually

```bash
# Capture a test alert
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> sh -c 'tail -1 /var/ossec/logs/alerts/alerts.json > /tmp/test_alert.json'

# Test the script (replace with your actual API key)
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/framework/python/bin/python3 /var/ossec/integrations/custom-w2thive.py /tmp/test_alert.json http://<STACK_IP>:9000 YOUR_API_KEY
```

### Monitor Integration Activity

```bash
# Watch integration logs in real-time
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> tail -f /var/ossec/logs/integrations.log

# Count alerts sent
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> grep -c "Create TheHive alert" /var/ossec/logs/integrations.log

# Check for errors
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> grep -i "error\|fail\|exception" /var/ossec/logs/integrations.log
```

### Check Alert Levels

```bash
# View alert level distribution
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> tail -100 /var/ossec/logs/alerts/alerts.json | grep -o '"level":[0-9]*' | sort | uniq -c

# Find high-severity alerts (level 7+)
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> grep '"level":7\|"level":8\|"level":9\|"level":1[0-9]' /var/ossec/logs/alerts/alerts.json | tail -5
```

### Update Integration Configuration

```bash
# Copy config out
docker cp <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name>:/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf ./ossec.conf

# Edit locally
nano ossec.conf

# Copy back
docker cp ossec.conf <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name>:/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf

# Restart
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-control restart
```

