## 7. Alert Generation & Testing

### Windows Alert Generation

#### Authentication Failures (Level 5-10)

```powershell
# Multiple failed logins
for ($i=1; $i -le 15; $i++) {
    runas /user:attacker123 "cmd.exe"
    Start-Sleep -Seconds 1
}
# Click Cancel on each prompt
```

#### Registry Modifications (Level 7-10)

```powershell
# Add Run key (persistence)
reg add "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run" /v MalwareTest /t REG_SZ /d "C:\temp\malware.exe" /f

# Disable UAC
reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System" /v EnableLUA /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
```

#### File Integrity Monitoring (Real-time)

```powershell
# Create file in monitored Startup folder
New-Item -Path "$env:PROGRAMDATA\Microsoft\Windows\Start Menu\Programs\Startup\backdoor.exe" -ItemType File -Force
```

#### Process Execution (Level 5-8)

```powershell
# Suspicious commands
net user
net localgroup administrators
net share

# PowerShell bypass
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "Write-Host 'Test'"
```

#### Service Manipulation (Level 8-10)

```powershell
# Create suspicious service
sc create MaliciousService binPath= "C:\temp\bad.exe"

# Stop security service
Stop-Service WinDefend -Force
```

### Verify Alerts Were Generated

```bash
# Check recent HYDRA-DC alerts
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> grep "HYDRA-DC" /var/ossec/logs/alerts/alerts.json | tail -10

# Check if alerts were sent to TheHive
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> tail -20 /var/ossec/logs/integrations.log
```

