## Common Issues & Solutions

### Issue: Container can't access internet

```bash
# Check host network
ping -c 3 8.8.8.8

# If host works, check container
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> ping -c 3 8.8.8.8

# Fix: Restart Docker networking
sudo systemctl restart docker
```

### Issue: thehive4py not found

```bash
# Install the module
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/framework/python/bin/pip3 install thehive4py==1.8.1

# Verify
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> /var/ossec/framework/python/bin/pip3 list | grep thehive
```

### Issue: Alerts not appearing in TheHive

```bash
# Check alert levels
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> tail -100 /var/ossec/logs/alerts/alerts.json | grep -o '"level":[0-9]*' | sort | uniq -c

# Lower threshold if needed (edit ossec.conf)
<level>5</level>  # Instead of 7

# Check integration logs
docker exec <your_Wazuh-manager_container_name> tail -f /var/ossec/logs/integrations.log
```

### Issue: Windows agent not connecting

```powershell
# Check service
Get-Service WazuhSvc

# Check logs
Get-Content "C:\Program Files (x86)\ossec-agent\ossec.log" -Tail 50

# Verify manager IP in config
Get-Content "C:\Program Files (x86)\ossec-agent\ossec.conf" | Select-String "address"
```

### Issue: Data lost after docker-compose down

```bash
# Verify volumes are mapped correctly in docker-compose.yml
# Data should persist in:
./thehive/data/
./cassandra/data/
./elasticsearch/data/

# Check if data exists
ls -lh ./thehive/data/
```

